---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<!--
  A stand-in for the real report. The deploy workflow (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) runs the test
  suite, builds the requirements traceability matrix with scripts/traceability.mjs, and replaces this
  page's output with it. This page exists so a local build has a page for the link on the This site
  project page to point at, and so the link checker finds one.
-->
<BaseLayout
  title="Requirements traceability report"
  description="Which requirements this site's Playwright tests verify, and the last result of each."
>
  <h1>Requirements traceability report</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The live site shows a matrix here: every requirement, the tests that verify it, and each one's last result. It is
    built when the site is deployed, so this local copy is only a stand-in.
  </p>
  <p>
    To build the matrix yourself, run <code>npm test</code>, then <code>npm run traceability</code>, and open
    <code>traceability/traceability.html</code>.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/development-qa/this-site/">Back to the This site page</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
